      "reasoning": "For q-76376, a₁+16d=33 and 2a₁+29d=1080/15=72. Subtracting twice the first equation from the second gives -3d=6, so d=-2 and a₁=65. For q-8461, comparison with the standard rotation matrix gives sin(theta)=-1/2 and cos(theta)=sqrt(3)/2, hence a clockwise rotation of pi/6 about the origin. The source's fourth-quadrant interval describes the nonnegative representative 11pi/6, equivalent modulo 2pi to the principal angle -pi/6. Both answers match their own captured worked solutions; the rotation answer also agrees with the earlier response. No captured grade was supplied.",
